# Mittal & Kumar 2003, figure 11: cylinder rotating at alpha = a omega/U, Re = 200,
# unsteady computation (filled circles; time averages and r.m.s. over the periodic
# state, for alpha >= 1.91 the flow is steady). Digitised from the bitmap
# (bitmapFigures_extract.py), ~0.3 % of the axis range. C_L(0) = 0 by symmetry,
# St(0) = 0.1934 and C_D(0) = 1.316 are in the text. C_P = C_D + C_M alpha (power
# coefficient), C_D, C_L, C_M normalised with rho U^2 a, rho U^2 a, rho U^2 a^2;
# St = f 2a/U; nan: not readable
